# The processes' memory on the least machine (roadmap memory.md M4, E3;
# disk-scheduler.md M8b): 639 or 640 KB of base memory and 384 KB above 1
# MB, an AT of 1 MB. tests/posix/many.c's 16 children of 60 KB, 1 MB of
# processes, cannot all fit: those that do are sound, and the others are
# told there is no memory, at their fork or at their malloc. How many fit
# is left open, as the image's code runs where it lies and each KB it grows
# is a KB less for them; none goes wrong.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_MANY
memory: 639K 384K
memory: 640K 384K
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 120
---
many: 16 children of 60 KB: forked {...}, refused {...}, sound {...}, no memory {...}, other 0
